{"name":"Far Horizons","hex":"#7fa2bf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"far","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Fataleka."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Distant; remote in space.","Remote in time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/far"},{"term":"horizons","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of horizon"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horizons"}],"entries":[{"title":"Far Horizons","blocks":[{"text":"Far Horizons: All New Tales from the Greatest Worlds of Science Fiction is an anthology of original science fiction stories edited by Robert Silverberg, first published in hardcover by Avon Eos in May 1999, with a book club edition following from Avon and the Science Fiction Book Club in July of the same year. Paperback and trade paperback editions were issued by Eos/HarperCollins in May 2000 and December 2005, respectively, and an ebook edition by HarperCollins e-books in March 2009. The first British edition was issued in hardcover and trade paperback by Orbit/Little Brown in June 1999, with a paperback edition following from Orbit in July 2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/Far-horizons-cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_Horizons"},{"title":"Far Horizons (Dublin, New Hampshire)","blocks":[{"text":"Far Horizons is a historic house located on Learned Road in Dublin, New Hampshire. Completed in 1899, it is a distinctive local example of Queen Anne architecture, and was home for a time to physicist Robert Kraichnan. The house was added to the National Register of Historic Places on December 15, 1983."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/DublinNH_FarHorizons.jpg/330px-DublinNH_FarHorizons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_Horizons_(Dublin%2C_New_Hampshire)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"far":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/En-uk-far.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e0/En-uk-far.ogg/En-uk-far.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-far.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ab/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-far.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-far.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ab/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-far.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-far.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ef/En-us-far.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ef/En-us-far.ogg/En-us-far.ogg.mp3"}]}}}